hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16832","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu al-Fadl al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, he said: And Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Dumayra narrated to me from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini from his grandfather Abu Hasan that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike secret marriage until the tambourine is beaten and it is said: We have come to you, we have come to you, so greet us and we will greet you."
"16833","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil, and he was a trustworthy righteous man, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, meaning al-Darawardi, narrated to us from Amr ibn Yahya from his father or his uncle, he said: I had a forelock, and when I prostrated I used to lift it, and Abu Hasan al-Mazini saw me and said: You lift it lest dust touch it; by Allah, I will surely shave it. And he shaved it."
"16834","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Hanafi Kathir ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Basri narrated to me, he said: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us from Ikrima ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, he said: A chief of the chiefs of Quraysh narrated to me from his father, he heard it from the mouth concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and Shawwal and Wednesday and Thursday will enter Paradise."
"16835","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me from his book, he said: Abu Isma'il al-Mu'addib informed us from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from Qays ibn A'idh, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching upon a slit-nosed she-camel, and an Abyssinian slave holding its halter. And Qays died in the days of al-Mukhtar."
